From 43df9eb2c9ef30ebd466c49c7dc2f31e13a63ce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:12:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(control-plane): run the controller in the
 application lifespan

Start a ControllerManager when the application starts and stop it on
shutdown, so resources created through the API are reconciled and get a
status that explains their state. Without a scheduler, which is the case
for every deployment today, a new InferenceService now reports
Ready=False with reason SchedulerUnavailable instead of staying Pending
forever.

- Dedup keys live in the same database file as the resources, so a
  restart neither loses pending work nor repeats side effects.
- DefaultPolicyEngine denies everything without rules; the application
  allows the "reconcile" action, since creating and deleting resources
  is already guarded by authentication and scopes.
- Startup and shutdown now use an AsyncExitStack, so a failure while
  starting the controller still closes the registry and resets the
  authenticator.

The controller is a single writer (ADR-013): run the application as a
single process and do not use uvicorn --workers.
